Thanks for your advice,

Indeed you said to fix hyperparameters, and this is the first unknown part i'm facing. In my model, 'dlm' assumes that the the observation variance is constant (unless i specified one or more "intervention"). In order to compare both approaches, is there a way in INLA to fix the observation variance?

Also thanks for your advice about reducing the nb of hyperparameters. What i think now is wrong in my current code is that i should have the same precision for cos and sin for each harmonic (but not all the same precision).

Thanks
Emmanuel

